  "body": "## What changed\n- A machine file can state `\"kind\": \"router\"`. The words \"CNC router\" and \"routing\" also work.\n- `Kind::from_word` reads a router word as `Kind::Mill`. A router keeps every mill rule.\n- The new `machine::is_router` reads the word as a router. A router is never inferred from the axes.\n- The new `camcraft_app::router_offer` module has one list of router options: `SheetJob` and `CornerRelief`.\n- A router offers all options. A machine that is not a router offers none. A project with no machine offers all.\n- The Setups page \"Sheet job\" group reads the list.\n- The corner relief rows on Pocket, 2D Adaptive and 2D Offset read the list.\n- A stated option stays shown on a mill. Nothing is hidden or deleted from a project.\n- MCP `get_job` reports `setups[].router_options` from the same function.\n- Six shipped files now state \"router\": Tormach 24R, xsTECH, xsTECH Pro, Sienci AltMill 2x4, 4x4, 4x8.\n- The refusal text for an unknown kind now names \"router\".\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2410-router-kind.md`.\n\n## Cause\nCamCraft had no router kind. A router file was a plain mill. So no page could show router options for a router only.\n\n## Design note\nThe escalation comment found that a new `Kind::Router` variant changes about 33 exhaustive matches in 5 crates. Each match can change posted G-code or a check. This PR uses a router word that reads as a mill. No match changes. No golden moves.\n\n## Tests\nNew pins:\n- `crates/app/tests/router_kind.rs`:\n  - `router_word_reads_as_a_mill`\n  - `shipped_routers_state_the_router_kind`\n  - `router_offers_the_router_options_and_a_mill_none`\n  - `mcp_get_job_reports_the_router_options_of_the_machine` (MCP list: router `[\"sheet_job\",\"corner_relief\"]`, mill `[]`)\n- `egui_app::tests::setup_settings_page::the_sheet_job_group_shows_on_a_router_and_not_on_a_mill` (UI)\n- `egui_app::tests::structural::corner_relief::relief_row_shows_on_a_router_and_not_on_a_mill` (UI)\n\nMutation checks (each guard put back alone, pin red, restored, pin green):\n- `setup_sheet_job_row.rs` from upstream/main: the Sheet job UI pin fails.\n- The corner relief guard disabled: the corner relief UI pin fails.\n- `mcp/job.rs` from upstream/main: the MCP pin fails (`left: Null`).\n- `tormach-24r.mch` from upstream/main: `shipped_routers_state_the_router_kind` and `router_offers_...` fail.\n- The router words removed from `from_word`: `router_word_reads_as_a_mill` fails.\n\nExpected-change tests: `plasma_machine::an_unknown_kind_is_still_refused` and `machine_library::other_stated_values_refuse_by_name` pin the refusal text. The text now names \"router\", so the two pins take the new text.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green after the two text pins. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone. No `.nc`, `.cl` or snapshot file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No router operation is hidden. The router uses the mill operation set. The function is the place to add one.\n- The tool-change macros of #2407 are post-defined and have no page control.\n- The machine editor Kind combo shows a router file as \"mill\". It writes the word only when the user changes the combo.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill text does not name the new field yet.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. The diff changes no geometry, toolpath or post code.\n\n## Overlaps\n- #3160 touches `crates/app/src/commands/setup_mount.rs`. This PR does not change that file.\n- #2890 and #2817 touch `crates/ui/src/egui_app/mill2d_page.rs`. This PR changes one call line in the Pocket passes tab. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\n## Follow-up\nEach open router sub-issue (#2398, #2399, #2401, #2402, #2404, #2405, #2406, #2408, #2409, Nest #2163) adds one `RouterOption` row and reads `router_offer::offers` on its page.\n\nChangelog: A machine file can state the kind \"router\"; a router shows the Sheet job group and corner relief, a mill hides them, and MCP `get_job` reports the router options.\n\nFixes #2410\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
